<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Las Anod</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Laascaanood</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Las Anod is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sool">Sool</a> region and the main town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhulbahante">Dhulbahante</a> clan. Contested between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a>, it was taken by Somaliland forces in 2007. In 2023 local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ssc-khatumo">SSC-Khatumo</a> forces fought the Somaliland army around the city and in August drove it from its positions, ending Somaliland's control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/las-anod.jpg" alt="Las Anod" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Siirski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laascaanood_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Setting</h2><p>Las Anod is the administrative capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sool">Sool</a> region, lying in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nugaal-valley">Nugaal Valley</a> along trade routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a>. The city is almost surrounded by hills and has considerable water resources, which has drawn people from the generally arid regions around it. It has a hot arid climate with almost no rain except erratically in May and October. It is inhabited mainly by people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> ethnic group, in particular the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhulbahante">Dhulbahante</a> sub-clan of the Harti Darod; the the UNFPA estimated the population of the district at 156,438 in 2014. Most of its goods arrive through the ports of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbera">Berbera</a> and Bosaso.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p>On 31 July 1903 thirty British scouts fought for two hours with the advance scouts of a party of 128 followers of the Mullah, a few miles west of Heli Madu near Las Anod. In the British protectorate era the town was capital of the Nogal District, the forerunner of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sool">Sool</a>. The United Somali Party was founded there to form a non-Isaaq axis, and from 1959 to 1961 it was the seat of Garad Ali's party. On 15 October 1969 Somali President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdirashid-ali-shermarke">Abdirashid Ali Shermarke</a> was shot dead by one of his bodyguards while visiting the city, and on 21 October a bloodless military coup led by Major General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siad-barre">Mohamed Siad Barre</a> seized power.</p><p>The city is disputed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puntland">Puntland</a>, whose claim rests on kinship between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhulbahante">Dhulbahante</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majeerteen">Majeerteen</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, whose claim rests on the border of the former British Somaliland Protectorate. Somaliland forces took it from Puntland forces in the Battle of Las Anod in 2007. In December 2022 the assassination of a local politician led to confrontations in which 20 protesters died, and in February 2023 war broke out between Somaliland and Khatumo State forces. Somaliland blamed al-Shabaab, while Nicholas Delaunay of the International Crisis Group said no concrete evidence had been provided. By 23 February the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> reported more than 185,000 people displaced. On 25 August 2023 Khatumo State forces drove Somaliland's forces out of Las Anod.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">The place today</h2><p>Las Anod is the centre of political power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhulbahante">Dhulbahante</a> clan. Nugaal University, founded in 2004, was the first institution of higher learning established in the area, and its first four-year students graduated in September 2009. Ilays National University and Gollis University were established in 2015. The city was the capital of Khatumo State until 2017, and its notable natives include the runner Abdi Bile.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Las Anod” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Puntland, the autonomous region of Somalia founded in 1998, disputes the Sool and Sanaag regions, whose Dhulbahante and Warsangeli clans are divided in their loyalties, and Somaliland forces took the town of <b>Las Anod</b> in 2007.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Republic of Somaliland · Military</a></li></ul></section>
